From: Togo Tagai <mail@mikan.observer>
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: bus: brcm,axi: add USB core quirks

Some Northstar boards need a DMU reset sequence before their USB 3.0
core is enabled, or a bounded settle period after the host child has been
removed.  Document optional properties for these board-level requirements.

Signed-off-by: Togo Tagai <mail@mikan.observer>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/bus/brcm,bus-axi.txt | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/bus/brcm,bus-axi.txt
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/bus/brcm,bus-axi.txt
@@ -19,6 +19,19 @@ The top-level axi bus may contain childr
 detected (e.g. IRQ numbers). Also some of the cores may be responsible
 for extra things, e.g. ChipCommon providing access to the GPIO chip.
 
+Optional properties for USB 3.0 cores:
+
+- brcm,usb3-dmu-syscon : phandle to the CRU syscon followed by the USB 3.0
+  DMU control register offset.  The BCMA USB host driver temporarily clears
+  and restores bits 3 and 4 before enabling the USB 3.0 core.  This sequence
+  is only performed when the property is present.
+
+- brcm,shutdown-delay-ms : delay in milliseconds after removing the USB host
+  child devices and before disabling the BCMA core. This is intended for
+  boards whose boot firmware requires the SuperSpeed link and attached device
+  to settle before reset. Values greater than 10000 are rejected by the
+  driver.
+
 Example:
 
 	axi@18000000 {
